Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"amy|Los Angeles? On a school night? I have thirty second-graders at eight.":"","deedee|Oh, Tommy. Somebody has to stay with my angels. And the pies.":"","deedee|Here. Cookies for the flight. To the moon and back, honey.":"","amy|Go. I will race you when you get back. And I will win.":"","boppy|Go on. The recliner and I will hold down the fort.":"","boppy|Six hours in a seat? My stomach says no. I say no. We agree for once.":"","tom|...I already miss the piggybacks.":"","tom|Delta One. Lie flat. Six whole hours where nobody asks me for a piggyback.":"","tom|TNB said he would be home. Spring Street loft. He is never home.":"","tom|Downtown LA. Seventy-two and sunny. It is always seventy-two and sunny.":"","tom|...He said he would be home.":"","tnb|Look who flew three thousand miles to see me.":"","tom|I flew three thousand miles to see my sourdough starter. You are a bonus.":"","tnb|I will take bonus. Bonus sounds premium. Like your seat.":"","tnb|My call time got pushed to Thursday. The lead actor lost a shoe. I already found it. So I am all yours.":"","tom|We will look. After I check on 2nd Ave. My starter has been alone for a week.":"","tnb|Also, something is up. The sky over Griffith Park went purple this morning. Not sunset purple. Weird purple.":"","tnb|Olivia dropped her off this morning. Family trip to the desert. No dogs at the hotel.":"","tnb|She has been sitting on your porch since eight. I tried to take her to the loft. She refused.":"","tom|Mad? I am proud. And a little mad.":"","tnb|Also, your starter was bubbling out of the jar, so I baked a boule with it. Do not be mad.":"","tom|Hello, Bready Mercury. Did you miss me? You missed me.":"","tom|Fifty grams of flour, fifty grams of water. Stir. Look at those bubbles. Proud of you.":"","tom|Sit, paw, treat. She knows the whole routine. Very polite. Very strong paw.":"","tnb|You talk to that jar more than you talk to me.":"","tom|The jar never leaves wet towels on the bed.":"","tnb|Fair. Very fair.":"","tnb|Babe. Look outside. Is the street... purple?":"","tom|Mr. Washington! Is everything okay?":"","tnb|He has been on \"this whole block\" for a while, babe.":"","washington|...":"","washington|Tom. Back in 1979, this whole block...":"","tom|Excuse me, smog. That was UNCALLED for.":"","washington|Such a nice afternoon. It should always be this afternoon.":"","mudling|Cough. Nice street. We are going to sit on it for a while. Forever, actually.":"","tom|I was startled. Briefly. With dignity.":"","tnb|Babe. Remember movie night? You threw the whole popcorn bowl.":"","tnb|It was a battle plan. You just did not know it yet.":"","tnb|They are gone, but he is still out of it. Look at him.":"","tnb|Okay. Okay. Everybody breathe. Through the nose. Not the smog.":"","washington|Nobody needs to go anywhere. Nobody needs to get any older.":"","tom|That is not a Mr. Washington sentence. Let us check on the boulevard. Miss Odette and Doña Carmen.":"","odette|Stirring. Stirring. The gumbo never has to be done, baby. Isn’t that nice?":"","tnb|She has made that gumbo every day for fifty years. It has never once been \"never done.\"":"","tom|The smog wants everything to stay exactly the same. Forever. That is not a nice afternoon. That is a hostage situation.":"","tnb|Nara is right. That is not kitchen smoke. That is the same purple stuff.":"","tnb|Babe. Look north. It is all coming down off the hills.":"","carmen|The pupusas are fine. Everything is fine. It is always this afternoon. Why would I ever flip them?":"","tom|Then that is where we are going. Nara, stay close.":"","tnb|The Observatory. The pipes on the side are pumping it out like a smoke machine on a bad set.":"","tnb|I take the Metro. You have nothing on me.":"","skeeter|Street cleaning. Tuesday. Eight to ten. You did not read the sign. And the smog says we can stay forever.":"","tnb|Up, everybody. Wardrobe says nobody is cut from this scene.":"","tom|Contested. Appeal granted. Keep going.":"","grump|Pack Howl. For the fluffy one.":"","grump|Nice hike. You look like you have snacks. And the dog looks like a snack.":"","tnb|Quick wardrobe adjustment, quick heal, and a quick kiss for the road. Ready, babe?":"","tom|Ready. The Observatory is up at the top left. Follow the purple.":"","tnb|The ground is humming. That is never a good sign. I have seen this movie forty-seven times.":"","bigone|RUMBLE. Somebody plugged my pipes. Now everything is stuck. I LIKE stuck.":"","bigone|Stuck means nothing moves. Nothing changes. Nothing ever has to say goodbye.":"","tom|Some of us have a six AM flight out of LAX. Things have to move.":"","tnb|Cut. Reset. Back to one, everybody.":"","tnb|Well, well, well... looks like we are in a bit of a shaky situation.":"","tnb|Babe, heal right after the Aftershock. When it clogs up, hit it with water or sparkle. Or one of our Tombos.":"","bigone|Rumble. You asked how I was doing. Nobody has asked in a million years.":"","bigone|...I will let things move. A little. Two inches a year. That is my best offer.":"","tnb|Look. The sky is blue again. LA blue. Slightly brown, but blue.":"","bigone|Rumble. Fine. The pipes are clear. I am going back under the hill to think about my choices.":"","tom|Somebody plugged those pipes on purpose. Smog does not do that by itself.":"","tnb|Spooky. I love it. I hate it. Let us go check on Mr. Washington.":"","washington|...smelled like gumbo on a Saturday night. Zydeco from the boulevard. Kids on every porch.":"","washington|Where was I? Oh. I was done. That was the whole story.":"","tom|Keep the old windows, though.":"","washington|Keep the old windows. Smart man.":"","washington|Funny. For a while there I did not want anything to change. Then I remembered the best parts all came from things changing.":"","tnb|Doña Carmen says the pupusas came out perfectly crispy. Miss Odette is sending over gumbo. The whole block is cooking.":"","bun|I'm filming a day-in-my-life video. I live in the lofts.":"","tom|Home. Both of them. Okay. Good.":"","bun|Say hi to my eleven followers.":"","bun|This is the day. You're in my life now.":"","bean|I'm an actor. Well. I'm an actor who parks cars at a tower.":"","bean|I had a callback last week. For a cereal.":"","bean|The cereal went with someone else. It happens.":"","page|I'm a screenwriter. I live in the lofts, two floors down from your boyfriend.":"","page|Draft forty-one. It's about a man who writes screenplays. It's very personal.":"","page|He lends me a mug when I am stuck. I am stuck a lot. I have nine of his mugs.":"","boomie|TOM! Get over here. Hug. Mmm-hmm. There it is.":"","boomie|Sorry, I sang that whole sentence. It happens. The lawyer on the bench has heard every note.":"","boomie|Are you eating? You look like you are not eating. I have a plate for you upstairs. Do not argue.":"","boomie|La la LAAA! Oops. A car alarm went off. That one is on me.":"","boomie|You text me when you land. I mean it. A song is also fine.":"","boomie|Sol says he times his breaks around my high notes. I say he times them around my cornbread.":"","boomie|I sang in the shower this morning. The whole building clapped. Thin walls.":"","boomie|How is TNB? How is that bread? Tell me everything. I have time.":"","boomie|Somebody on the ninth floor was having a bad day. I sang them a little something. Now it is a medium day.":"","boomie|Same age, same jokes, Tom. I just hit the high notes.":"","pip|I came all the way from Ohio. I rode the tiny orange railway up the hill.":"","boomie|Hmm hmm hmmm. Oh, I was humming? I am always humming.":"","pip|It went one block. It cost a dollar. Best dollar of my life.":"","pip|Then I ate a pupusa in a market from 1917. I may never go home.":"","olivia|Tom! You kept Nara alive! Did she eat? She did not eat, did she.":"","olivia|The desert was gorgeous. Lachlan found a rock. Isla ate a rock. Different rock.":"","olivia|MICHAEL. Can you grab Isla? She is going for the dog bowl.":"","olivia|Tom! Hi! Sorry, I am mid-sentence in my head. I am filing a story on AI in classrooms.":"","olivia|MICHAEL. Can you grab Isla? She has a leaf. She is going to eat the leaf.":"","olivia|The kids use it to write the homework. The teachers use it to grade the homework. Nobody is in the room.":"","olivia|My editor wants a piece on AI taking jobs. I said I would write it myself. While I still can.":"","olivia|Michael, can you take Lachlan? He is licking the fence. Thank you, babe.":"","olivia|Everybody asks if robots will take their jobs. I tell them a robot still cannot fold a fitted sheet. Neither can I.":"","olivia|I interviewed a chatbot today. It was very polite. Too polite. I did not trust it.":"","olivia|Michael! Isla is near the curb. Okay. He has her. He always has her.":"","olivia|Did Nara eat today? Tell me the truth. Michael, did Nara eat?":"","olivia|Teachers are not getting replaced. They are getting a very confident new student who never did the reading.":"","michael|Hey, Tom. I would wave, but I am out of arms.":"","michael|I work at Meta. I build things that connect people. Right now I am connecting a four-year-old to a nap.":"","michael|I heard Olivia say Michael. I am already holding them. I am always holding them.":"","michael|Yes, Olivia. Got him. Got her. Got both. I have had both since breakfast.":"","michael|Lachlan wants to know if Nara is his dog. I said it is complicated. It is not. It is his dog.":"","michael|Isla said her first word last week. It was no. She uses it very well.":"","michael|I took a meeting today with Isla on my lap. She muted me. Best meeting of the quarter.":"","michael|My arms have never been stronger. I have not lifted a weight in four years.":"","washington|Back in 1979, this whole block...":"","michael|Olivia writes about AI taking jobs. Nobody is coming for mine. Nobody wants bedtime.":"","washington|Such a nice afternoon. It should always be this afternoon. Nobody needs to get any older.":"","washington|Where was I? Oh. 1979. This whole block smelled like gumbo on a Saturday night.":"","washington|That smog had me stuck on one sentence for an hour. At my age I do not have hours to spare.":"","washington|Thank you, Tom. And your young man. And the dog. Especially the dog.":"","washington|Bought this house in 1979. Same porch, same chair, same view.":"","washington|Back then you could hear zydeco from the boulevard on a Saturday night.":"","washington|You are the one fixing up the green house? Keep the old windows. They are better than the new ones.":"","la_woman|I am walking my dog. I have always been walking my dog.":"","la_woman|I will always be walking my dog. Isn't that nice?":"","la_woman|I'm walking my dog. He's somewhere.":"","la_woman|There he is. No. That is a lemon.":"","la_woman|My grandparents rented on this block. Now I rent on this block. We are a tradition.":"","gus|I am blowing leaves. The same leaf. Over and over.":"","gus|Onto the next yard.":"","gus|It never lands. It never has to. Very peaceful.":"","gus|I'm blowing leaves.":"","gus|Tomorrow, they blow them back. It's a whole system.":"","luna|Our oat milk is oat-adjacent.":"","luna|Welcome to Golden Hour. Every hour is golden hour if you believe.":"","luna|Your name is Tom? I wrote TAM. It is basically the same.":"","kenji|Irasshaimase! Welcome!":"","kenji|Tom-san, your Japanese is very good.":"","kenji|It is not. But you are trying very hard, and I respect that.":"","fern|Welcome. Breathe in. Now order.":"","fern|We opened in March. The pupuseria next door has been here since 1994. We are learning a lot.":"","moss|Board Room. We sell boards. We also sit on them.":"","fern|Today's special is celery. Doña Carmen says that is not a meal. She is right.":"","moss|TNB? Longboard guy? He bombed Fargo Street once. No brakes. Legend.":"","moss|If you see him, tell him the wheels he ordered came in. The green ones.":"","moss|I've been in this chair since the game started. Which game? Yes.":"","moss|Ten people. I counted once. Then I lost count. Then I took a nap.":"","la_woman|Baby Lupita is finally asleep. If you wake her, you are moving in.":"","la_woman|Sofi, no. Sofi. SOFI. ...She bit something. We do not have a dog. I do not know what she bit.":"","luna|Night shift nurse. I sleep in the bathtub. It is the only room with a lock.":"","luna|Until somebody needs the bathroom. Somebody always needs the bathroom.":"","tnb|Hey, you. Did you eat? I made a bowl. I also made a bowl. Pottery joke.":"","tnb|Take my jacket. It gets cold up in Griffith Park at night, and a cold Tom is a no-go.":"","tnb|Took the longboard down Spring Street this morning. Smooth. There is a crack by Fourth Street I have named.":"","tnb|Welcome to the loft. Kiln by one window, wheel by the other, garment bags everywhere else. Spring Street, baby.":"","tnb|Go on, I will be right here. I am pot-sitive about it.":"","tnb|Threw six mugs this morning. The glaze came out of the kiln like sea glass. Come look before you claim one.":"","tnb|Horror movie tonight. You pick. You always pick the scary one and then hold my arm the whole time.":"","tnb|Watered your plants on 2nd Ave. The fern asked about you. I said you are fine.":"","tnb|Rode the train to the clay studio. Forty minutes. Best forty minutes of my day. Met a man who knows every line.":"","tnb|The slime? It just needs someone to mold it. I have more of these. You know I do.":"","tnb|Be careful out there. I like you un-cracked.":"","tnb|Long day on set. Eleven costume changes. One actor lost a shoe. I found it. I always find it.":"","dot|34th floor. From my desk I can see Griffith Park. I have never been to Griffith Park.":"","dot|My dog is named Bagel. He has more friends in this building than I do.":"","odette|Stirring. Stirring.":"","dot|The pool is on the roof. Nobody swims. Everyone takes photos of the pool.":"","odette|The gumbo never has to be done, baby. Isn't that nice? Nothing ever has to be done.":"","odette|Sit. Eat. You and that boyfriend earned a bowl today.":"","odette|That smog had me stirring one pot for an hour. Best roux I ever made, though.":"","odette|Sit down, baby. Gumbo's on. It's been on since six.":"","odette|My mama opened this kitchen when this stretch was Little New Orleans. Folks came from Louisiana and brought the food.":"","carmen|The pupusas are fine. Everything is fine.":"","odette|Pralines by the register. Take two. One for you, one for that boyfriend who keeps coming in for the red beans.":"","carmen|It is always this afternoon. Why would I ever flip them?":"","carmen|Do not tell the juice bar. They will want the recipe.":"","carmen|I left them on the comal the whole time. They came out perfectly crispy, actually.":"","carmen|Bienvenidos! Pupusas revueltas, and curtido on the side. Curtido is not optional.":"","carmen|I came from San Salvador in 1991. This comal came with me in a suitcase.":"","carmen|The juice bar next door asked me what a pupusa is. I gave them three. Now they ask every day.":"","pip|Mrs. Alvarez brought us tamales. We posted them. We tagged her. She does not have Instagram.":"","pip|Our mortgage is, um. We don't say the number out loud. The house can hear.":"","pip|Everyone else on this street rents. We think about that a lot. Mostly on podcasts.":"","dot|We're restoring the original 1912 windows. It's a whole thing.":"","dot|Every house on this street has a story. Ours is: the plumbing.":"","dot|Mr. Washington told us the windows are older than his father. He was very serious about it.":"","bean|Baby Hudson is asleep. Please whisper. Please. I am begging.":"","bean|We moved from the Westside for the space. And the character. Mostly the price. Which was still a lot.":"","bean|I work from home. Home is very loud on the Alvarez side. I bought noise-canceling headphones. They lost.":"","mudling|Cough. You can see the hills? Not for long.":"","mudling|I came from a tailpipe on the 101. I am very proud.":"","mudling|Traffic picked up. So did I.":"","mudling|Round 2. I brought my cousins from the 405.":"","mudling|Round 3. I brought my cousins from the 405.":"","mudling|Round 4. I brought my cousins from the 405.":"","mudling|Round 5. I brought my cousins from the 405.":"","mudling|...I am waiting for rush hour. Then I will be back.":"","mudling|Cough. Give me a minute. Cough.":"","skeeter|We doubled. Late fees.":"","skeeter|Street cleaning. Tuesday. Eight to ten. You did not read the sign.":"","skeeter|We are seventy-three dollars each. There are a lot of us.":"","skeeter|Round 2. Your appeal was denied.":"","skeeter|Round 3. Your appeal was denied.":"","skeeter|Round 4. Your appeal was denied.":"","skeeter|Round 5. Your appeal was denied.":"","skeeter|Contested. Pending review.":"","skeeter|We are being processed. Come back in six to eight weeks.":"","grump|Nice hike. You look like you have snacks.":"","grump|I have been running the fire roads.":"","grump|I live here. You are visiting. Remember that.":"","grump|Round 2. I told the others about you.":"","grump|Round 3. I told the others about you.":"","grump|Round 4. I told the others about you.":"","grump|...I am lying in the sun. Leave me alone.":"","grump|Round 5. I told the others about you.":"","grump|Come back after dark. I am better after dark.":"","grump|HONK. The 405 sent me.":"","grump|You are in my lane. Everyone is in my lane.":"","grump|I found a shortcut. It was worse.":"","grump|Round 3. Lane closures ahead.":"","grump|Round 2. Lane closures ahead.":"","grump|Round 4. Lane closures ahead.":"","grump|...SigAlert. Do not come this way.":"","grump|Round 5. Lane closures ahead.":"","grump|I am parked. Leave a note.":"","mudling|Everything that steps in me stays a while.":"","mudling|Glorp. I found another bone.":"","mudling|Glorp. I have had mammoths. You are not a mammoth.":"","mudling|Round 3. I am stickier now.":"","mudling|Round 2. I am stickier now.":"","mudling|Round 4. I am stickier now.":"","mudling|Round 5. I am stickier now.":"","mudling|...Glorp. Ten thousand years is a long nap.":"","mudling|I am resting. Like a fossil.":"","bigone|RUMBLE. Everyone says I am overdue.":"","bigone|Rumble. I moved two inches. That is a lot for me.":"","bigone|I have been under this city for a million years. Nobody has ever been ready.":"","bigone|Round 2. Drop, cover, and hold on.":"","bigone|Round 3. Drop, cover, and hold on.":"","bigone|Round 4. Drop, cover, and hold on.":"","bigone|Round 5. Drop, cover, and hold on.":"","bigone|...Rumble. That was a foreshock. Probably.":"","bigone|I am settling. Do not stand near the bookshelves.":"","tnb|Not right now, babe.":"","tnb|Tom, your shoelace. No, the other one. Got it.":"","tnb|If a coyote jumps out at us, I have seen this movie. Stay together. Nobody go in the basement.":"","tnb|Well, well... a foggy canyon at dusk. This is how every horror movie starts.":"","tnb|After this, clay. Any two colors. I will make them get along.":"","penny|Welcome to Nickel's. I am Penny's cousin. Better weather, same prices.":"","penny|Got something to sell? I buy almost anything. Penny warned me about Steve.":"","penny|Gear for the whole family, snacks for fights, sunscreen for the soul.":"","penny|Fresh stock. Same Nickel.":"","penny|Back again! Did you find parking? Nobody finds parking.":"","penny|Browse all you like. Browsing is free in Los Angeles. Nothing else is.":"","oolong|Backlot Wardrobe. If it was worn on screen, it lived here first.":"","oolong|We still talk about the shoe. Tell him there is always a rack here with his name on it.":"","oolong|You're Tom? TNB's Tom! He found a shoe for us once. A lead actor's shoe. Four minutes before the take.":"","ellie|Welcome to the Starlite. Built in 1931. The popcorn is newer. A little.":"","ellie|I have run the projector here for forty years. I have seen every movie twice.":"","sal|Angel City Cab Co. I am Sol. Sal's cousin. Also one cab.":"","ellie|Tonight it is a horror double feature. Your boyfriend would love it. You would watch it through your fingers.":"","sal|Cab eight. Sal has cab seven. We do not talk about what happened to the other six.":"","sal|I go to the airport, the airport, and sometimes the airport.":"","sal|Where to? The airport? It is always the airport.":"","sal|Okay. I will be here. In traffic.":"","kit|We took it down to the studs. Then we put the studs back. Very authentic.":"","kit|Have you tried the juice bar on Jefferson? It's so nice the neighborhood is finally getting... options.":"","kit|We painted it black. The neighbors call it the haunted house. We are choosing to take that as a compliment.":"","sal|Go find your boyfriend. He called here twice asking if you landed.":"","sal|Airport? You JUST landed. The smog has me grounded anyway. I cannot see the freeway.":"","carmen|TEN. Ten people in a two-bedroom house from 1912. One bathroom. ONE.":"","carmen|Tony, feet off my table! Kevin, the baby is not a football! Mateo, give Abuela the remote! ...Tom, mijo, sit. If you can find a chair.":"","carmen|Everybody says, 'Mama, the house is so full of love.' It is full of SOMETHING. Take tamales. Please. I need the room in my fridge.":"","bean|I share the bunk bed with Uncle Tony's exercise bike.":"","michael|Me and Yesenia are saving for our own place. In this market? We will be here until Mateo goes to college.":"","michael|The two houses next door sold for more than this whole block cost in 1990. My mom is not okay about it.":"","bean|It is not a metaphor. The bike is on the top bunk.":"","rose|I'm making a documentary about this house. It's a horror movie.":"","rose|Scene one: the bathroom line. Scene two: who ate Abuela's last concha.":"","bean|Truck! TRUCK!":"","bean|Ba! Ba! ...Truck.":"","rose|I'm a dinosaur. RAWR.":"","rose|Abuela says no more dinosaurs inside. I'm a quiet dinosaur. rawr.":""});
Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.voices,{"deedee":{"voice_id":"0mLOQqwA3kovxF1ID7z6","name":"Linda – Gentle Mom Storytime Voice  (female, old, canadian, narrative_story)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"amy":{"voice_id":"VCUa8W1mPO0QcgrSewvs","name":"Carolina - Clear and Straightforward  (female, middle_aged, new york, informative_educational)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"boppy":{"voice_id":"QzTKubutNn9TjrB7Xb2Q","name":"Jerry B. - New York Italian Mobster  (male, middle_aged, new york, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":1},"direction":"deep gravelly voice","designed":false},"tom":{"voice_id":"cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal","name":"Eric - Smooth, Trustworthy","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"tnb":{"voice_id":"QPmHuIriDGOvu1d9U7wn","name":"SuperDale - a mid-age voice & Friendly  (male, middle_aged, us midwest, informative_educational)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"washington":{"voice_id":"ARRjeRIXQjOrcraWRDoq","name":"AoT Mr. Washington","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly man in his eighties with a deep, warm, slow voice and a gentle hint of Louisiana in it. A neighborhood storyteller on his porch, unhurried, kind, a little gravelly. Clean studio recording."},"mudling":{"voice_id":"E2hOWZ8x3nGJuQURP3SG","name":"AoT Mudling","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small, silly cartoon creature made of mud, gloopy gurgling voice with wet bubbly consonants, slow and sulky, childlike and a little sad. Animated character voice."},"odette":{"voice_id":"ubIjwev8dFIC3TyJqJPC","name":"AoT Miss Odette","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her seventies with a rich, warm, musical voice and a light Louisiana Creole accent. Runs a soul food kitchen, calls everyone baby, unhurried and loving with a sly sense of humor. Clean studio recording."},"carmen":{"voice_id":"8ncJvaxiyfELP457mBLS","name":"AoT Doña Carmen","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her sixties with a warm, firm, proud voice and a light Salvadoran Spanish accent. Runs a pupuseria, generous and no-nonsense, laughs easily. Clean studio recording."},"skeeter":{"voice_id":"3NkCp1SubvPIw3g0s7Rf","name":"AoT Skeeter Swarm","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon swarm of mosquitoes speaking as one, high-pitched, thin, whiny and buzzy voice with a nasal zzz on every s, nosy and impatient. Animated character voice."},"grump":{"voice_id":"moX2FuSiiLmOw0uEq4OU","name":"AoT Pond Grump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A grumpy cartoon swamp creature, low gravelly grumbling voice, cranky and wet-sounding, easily offended, a big softie underneath. Animated character voice."},"bigone":{"voice_id":"qDteMRfOWoUEc7kcfWvl","name":"AoT The Big One","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An enormous ancient cartoon pond fish, huge slow booming bass voice with gurgling bubbles, pompous and boastful but childlike and easily delighted underneath. Animated character voice."},"bun":{"voice_id":"FSFvvh3OTPle9DfVJIu3","name":"AoT Bun","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her thirties with a bubbly, warm, bright American voice. Friendly shop greeter energy, smiling while she talks, loves a bread pun. Clean studio recording."},"bean":{"voice_id":"zROpM0X5rfQMe4CN4C7f","name":"AoT Bean","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his late twenties with an upbeat, rambling, friendly American voice. A little scattered, quick bursts of words, cheerful and unbothered. Light and bright. Clean studio recording."},"page":{"voice_id":"UnNThlnnIcLaHiWDpFdl","name":"AoT Page","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his forties, a librarian with a hushed, dry, whispery American voice. Speaks very quietly and precisely, mildly scandalized by everything, droll. Soft breathy whisper. Clean studio recording."},"boomie":{"voice_id":"FgGtmhYdBou3a14mKYgx","name":"AoT Boomie","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a big, warm, rich singer’s voice, bubbly and motherly, slides into song mid-sentence, laughs from the belly. Clean studio recording."},"pip":{"voice_id":"BI45NIQbK17XdpKBL2Kq","name":"AoT Pip","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A young woman in her twenties with a soft, earnest, slightly breathy American voice. Sweet and a little odd, very sincere, speaks gently and protectively like she is talking about a beloved pet. Clean studio recording."},"olivia":{"voice_id":"3KdkB2LF6PUw0muuS0j7","name":"AoT Olivia","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her late thirties with a quick, bright, articulate American voice. A journalist and mom of two little kids, talks fast, wry and warm, always half distracted. Clean studio recording."},"michael":{"voice_id":"24fSFWvKYGI0zVR7L6JQ","name":"AoT Michael","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A tall man in his early forties with a calm, low, dry American voice. A tech dad holding two kids, patient, deadpan, quietly funny, a little tired. Clean studio recording."},"la_woman":{"voice_id":"eLXwnyHT9UJHbuyheJ9m","name":"AoT LA neighbor (woman)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her early thirties with a relaxed, warm, slightly husky Los Angeles voice. Easygoing, wry, a little tired, friendly neighbor energy. Clean studio recording."},"gus":{"voice_id":"CcabrpeMRBXae9HlsCuq","name":"AoT Gus","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An old man in his seventies with a slow, warm, slightly creaky American voice. Deadpan and dignified, treats sitting on a bench like serious athletic training. Unhurried. Clean studio recording."},"luna":{"voice_id":"qCj5kMANfHcvCnzG1gVB","name":"AoT Luna","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her thirties with a dreamy, slow, wonder-filled American voice. Soft and spacey, drifting pauses, sincere awe with a touch of embarrassment. Clean studio recording."},"kenji":{"voice_id":"GsNjFqTDXKGM2xXbaGdG","name":"AoT Kenji","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his fifties with a warm, friendly, energetic voice and a light Japanese accent. A ramen shop owner, kind and honest, gently teasing. Clean studio recording."},"fern":{"voice_id":"P7lvbZpxKLc3X7wUPzDe","name":"AoT Fern","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her thirties with a gentle, airy, soothing American voice. Calm and earthy like she is talking to plants, soft and kind, quietly funny. Clean studio recording."},"moss":{"voice_id":"7vp7iK3I8DiDLgC90c3t","name":"AoT Moss","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A tall, gentle man in his thirties with a deep, slow, mellow American voice. Dreamy and laid back, long pauses, quietly pleased with his own puns. Warm low tone. Clean studio recording."},"dot":{"voice_id":"gYzudf4C0nXnEecqXK5t","name":"AoT Dot","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small woman in her forties with a quick, crisp, precise American voice, slightly nasal. Talks fast in short exact phrases like she is reading a tally sheet. Proud of her accuracy. Clean studio recording."},"penny":{"voice_id":"C0jocNoR6bwrjLXwelto","name":"AoT Penny","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her forties with a fast-talking, bright, enthusiastic American saleswoman voice. Quick patter, playful, warm and a little pushy, every line a pitch. Clean studio recording."},"oolong":{"voice_id":"2PhKaj7sDKqdDEhqQyhl","name":"AoT Oolong","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An elderly woman in her seventies with a warm, gossipy, conspiratorial voice and a light British accent. Leans in to share secrets, little cackle of a laugh, cozy and sly. Clean studio recording."},"ellie":{"voice_id":"rnhEc2YmD7cQEaA4v9MM","name":"AoT Aunt Ellie","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A very elderly woman in her nineties with a grand, theatrical, sharp-witted voice and a refined mid-Atlantic accent. Dry, imperious and glamorous, slow deliberate delivery, every line a bon mot. Clean studio recording."},"sal":{"voice_id":"gcJ5PkVgShIxtP5HgbZK","name":"AoT Sal","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his fifties with a thick Long Island New York accent, a slightly nasal, raspy, fast and friendly voice. Chatty taxi driver, warm and a little dramatic, proud of his one cab. Clean studio recording."},"rose":{"voice_id":"ocZQ262SsZb9RIxcQBOj","name":"Lulu Lolipop - High-Pitched and Bubbly  (female, young, american, characters_animation)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"kit":{"voice_id":"HrV34VWBLBZGZIRRrEuR","name":"AoT Kit","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his thirties with a chipper, brisk, friendly American voice. A cheerful mail carrier, upbeat and quick, with a wink in every sentence. Clean studio recording."}});
